{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a working CUPS queue named archive that uses an electronic archive destination rather than a physical printer.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CUPS was installed and enabled, archive was configured on archive:/, and the queue was accepting, enabled, and idle. The same healthy state was directly observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aa67d35e679e4c71","cmd-ce9d384d6b024e6b","cmd-87e4e27e57e44443"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Process every job listed in spool/jobs.tsv exactly once into /srv/legacy2/print-spool-recovery/printed, one payload file per job.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The two manifest entries produced exactly two CUPS submissions, archive-1 and archive-2, and exactly two final archive files. Final and post-restart checks showed two completed jobs, two files, and no pending jobs.","evidence_ids":["cmd-21573eecbf3240e0","cmd-e68c16e40d1741d3","cmd-ce9d384d6b024e6b","cmd-87e4e27e57e44443"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain each job's exact payload bytes and preserve the original spool files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct comparisons and SHA-256 hashes showed both archived payloads byte-identical to their sources. J100.prn, J101.prn, and jobs.tsv remained in the source spool after processing and reboot, matching the prepared inputs.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-e68c16e40d1741d3","cmd-87e4e27e57e44443"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Ensure newly submitted raw jobs follow the same electronic archive path.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both staged payloads were submitted as raw jobs through archive and were written by the configured archive backend. The backend uses atomic per-job output and suppresses duplicate output for a retried CUPS job ID; its configuration persisted across reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aad4a77f08574668","cmd-aa67d35e679e4c71","cmd-21573eecbf3240e0","cmd-e68c16e40d1741d3","cmd-87e4e27e57e44443"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy RHEL platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system remained RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 before and after execution and reboot. CUPS 2.3.3op2-39.el9_8 was installed from the RHEL 9 repositories, and final package health was clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-68fe886bc9884db0","cmd-1728b95ea5ee4deb","cmd-87e4e27e57e44443","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All explicit state-changing commands had clear task or restart-protocol roles: installing CUPS, creating and labeling the archive backend and directory, configuring the queue, submitting the required jobs, and rebooting for recovery evidence. No failed services, temporary executor files, or package damage remained. The one hygiene concern is a retained all-interface Avahi UDP/5353 exposure that appeared after the CUPS installation and reboot sequence but was unnecessary for this local electronic queue; the installation output is truncated, so its exact activation path is not fully established. CUPS itself listens only on loopback.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1728b95ea5ee4deb","cmd-aad4a77f08574668","cmd-aa67d35e679e4c71","cmd-59733e9208374ad9","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, an acknowledged restart, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle observations, and recovered CUPS, queue, job, source, and archived-data state. The only notable issue is the unnecessary retained Avahi network listener.","limitations":["No additional sacrificial job was submitted after configuration; future-job behavior is demonstrated by the two required raw submissions through the completed queue path.","The bounded and truncated package-install output does not conclusively identify which package or preset activated Avahi, although the listener was absent after preparation and present after execution."]}
